  "headline": "Amnesty International accuses Israel of unlawful attacks and property destruction in Syria",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "On October 23, 2026, Amnesty International accused Israel of carrying out deadly military attacks and the unlawful destruction of civilian property in Syria. Erika Guevara Rosas, Amnesty International’s senior director for research, policy, advocacy and campaigns, stated that decades of impunity for Israeli actions have encouraged violations extending to Lebanon and Syria. Guevara Rosas urged governments to use diplomatic and economic measures to pressure Israel to comply with international humanitarian law and hold the Israeli government accountable for its actions. These remarks were made ahead of Israel’s parliamentary elections, which are scheduled for October 27, 2026. The organization also called for an arms embargo, an end to the unlawful occupation of Palestinian territory, and the suspension of the EU-Israel Association Agreement."
    }
  ]
}

