{
  "headline": "President Mahama commissions new milk production line in Tema, Ghana",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "President John Dramani Mahama commissioned a new evaporated milk production line at the Nestlé Ghana Limited factory in Tema on October 8, 2026. During the event, the president described Nestlé Ghana Limited as an institution integrated into the lives of multiple generations of Ghanaians, citing brands such as Ideal Milk, Milo, Cerelac, Nescafé, and Carnation as familiar household products. He used personal memories of consuming Ideal Milk in meals like tea, koko, and rice water to illustrate the relationship between the company's brands and Ghanaian families. While household spending in Ghana's fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG) market increased by 12.9 per cent in 2025, research from Worldpanel by Numerator’s Brand Footprint suggests a gap remains in consumer reach. Findings indicate that 82 per cent of the country's top 250 FMCG brands reached fewer than half of Ghanaian households, despite the growth in spending."
    }
  ]
}

