  {"text": "Three residents of Amjhol village were injured in a tiger attack on Sunday evening near the Amjhol border in Hatibandha upazila, Lalmonirhat, Bangladesh, according to reports from UNB cited by The Financial Express. The animal reportedly crossed into Bangladesh from India near the border area, which falls under the jurisdiction of the Bonchouki Border Outpost in Gotamari Union. Local reports state that Sharifa Begum was attacked by the tiger while searching for a goat; Afsar Hossain and Nazrul Islam were also injured while attempting to rescue her. The three individuals were taken to a local hospital and subsequently transferred to Rangpur Medical College Hospital for advanced treatment. Lieutenant Colonel Mehedi Imam, commander of the Lalmonirhat 15 BGB Battalion, confirmed the injuries and stated that the Forest Department had been informed and security in the area had been strengthened."}
